-- title:
--   Lemma 8.20 — $H(N)$ is a canonical tree-decomposition when short cycles generate
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a locally finite, connected graph whose binary cycle space is generated by cycles of length at most $r$, let $k\in\mathbb N$, and let $N$ be a nested set of $r$-local separations of $G$ whose separators are $r$-tomic and of size at most $k$. Then $H(N)$ is a tree-decomposition (with parts) of $G$. Moreover, if $N$ is $\Gamma$-canonical for a subgroup $\Gamma\le\operatorname{Aut}(G)$, then $H(N)$ is $\Gamma$-canonical.
--
--   Applied in $G_r$, this makes $H(\hat N)$ a tree-decomposition that can be folded back to $G$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - reading: the binary cycle space of $G$ is generated by cycles of length $\le r$ → every cycle's edge set is a finite symmetric difference of edge sets of cycles of length $\le r$ (`CycleSpaceGenByShort`); reason: the finite cycle space; the proofs (Lemma 4.3, Correspondence 4.4) argue with finite $\mathbb Z/2$ sums
--   - reading: $s \succ t$ (used without a separate definition) and crossing/$\succcurlyeq$ defined for $r$-local separations with $r$-tomic separators → $s \succ t$ is $s \succcurlyeq t \wedge s \ne t$; the crossing and $\succcurlyeq$ conditions are defined for all pairs; reason: strict part of $\succcurlyeq$, as $>$ for $\geqslant$ in §8.1; the statement only applies them to separations with $r$-tomic separators
--   - encoding: orders $|X|$ of separators → `Set.encard` in $\mathbb N_\infty$; reason: separators of the infinite cover can be infinite (p.29); no finite instance changes
--   - encoding: $G$ locally finite → every neighbour set is finite (a `Prop`, not Mathlib's data-carrying `LocallyFinite` class); reason: same graphs
-- source:
--   Jacobs, Knappe, Kurkofka, Canonical Graph Decompositions via Local Separations, preprint (STOC 2027 submission, arXiv:2501.16170; sha256 9a11d48d…), Lemma 8.20, p.55

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_LocalSepDecomp_Cutouts

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace LocalSepDecomp

open SimpleGraph

universe u

/-- **Lemma 8.20.** R. W. Jacobs, P. Knappe, J. Kurkofka, *Canonical Graph Decompositions via Local Separations*,
preprint (STOC 2027 submission, arXiv:2501.16170; sha256 9a11d48d…), Lemma 8.20, p.55.
Let `G` be a locally finite, connected graph whose binary cycle space is generated by cycles of
length `≤ r`, and let `N` be a nested set of `r`-local separations of `G` with `r`-tomic separators
all of size `≤ k`. Then `H(N)` is a tree-decomposition (with parts) of `G`. Moreover, if `N` is
`Γ`-canonical, then so is `H(N)`. -/
theorem lemma_8_20 {V : Type u} (G : SimpleGraph V) (hlf : IsLocallyFinite G)
    (hG : G.Connected) (r : ℕ) (hcyc : CycleSpaceGenByShort G r) (k : ℕ) (N : Set (ULSep V))
    (hN : ∀ u ∈ N, IsULSep G r u ∧ IsRTomic G r u.X ∧ u.X.encard ≤ k)
    (hnest : ULSetNested G r N) :
    IsTreeDecomp (Hdecomp G r N) ∧
      ∀ Γ : Subgroup (G ≃g G), IsCanonicalULSepSet G Γ N →
        IsCanonicalDecomp Γ (Hdecomp G r N) := by sorry

end LocalSepDecomp
